==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Ram|Raum|Rohm|Rom|Room}} {{q|all obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Dialectal variant of expected {{m|de|Raum}} (early modern German, rare), from {{inh|de|gmh|roum}}, from {{inh|de|goh|roum}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*raum}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*raumaz}}. 

The form {{m|de||Rahm}} ousted the regular form due to homonymy with {{m|de|Raum|t=room}}, from {{noncog|gmh|rūm}}. Dialects that have developed Middle High German ''-ou-'' into ''-ā-'' are found in south-eastern and central-western Germany. Cognate with {{cog|nl|room}} and {{cog|en|ream}}.

